Explosives will now shake ore loose from rock.

1) A TNT blast in hills, mountains or a cave reveals ore.
   - What comes out is what a pick would have found there, so depth and
     sector still decide it.
   - The chunks land on the floor for whoever is still standing.

2) How much depends on the size of the charge.
   - The blast level is rolled as a percentage, then eight less, then
     eight less again, each its own chance at another chunk.
   - A small charge usually shakes nothing loose.  A large one opens a
     seam.

3) A blast works a face as hard as a day of swinging.
   - It carries the same chance of finishing the room off.

